    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n4431" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">auctumnus</span></b>  (correctly <b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">aut-</span></b> ), a, um, adj.
		1. auctumnus, <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b><i>autumnal</i> (<b>poet.</b> or in
			post-Aug. prose): 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">imber,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Cato, R. R. 58</span></i>
			: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">autumno frigore,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Ov. M.
					3, 729</span></i>
			 (Merk., <i>autumni frigore</i>): 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">sidera,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Manil. 2, 269</span></i>
			: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">tempus,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">id. 2, 425</span></i>
			: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">pruinae,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Aus. Idyll. 8, 10</span></i>
			; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">Cod. Th. 2, 8, 2: aequinoctium,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Plin.
					19, 6, 33, § 108</span></i>
			: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">tempestas,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Gell.
					19, 7, 2</span></i>
			.</div>
